          ],
          "component_type": "data_center",
          "metric_value": "240",
          "unit": "$M",
          "source_quote": "ARMONK, N.Y. and SAN FRANCISCO , Aug. 11, 2026 / PRNewswire / -- IBM (NYSE: IBM ) announced a collaboration with Together AI to deliver IBM and NVIDIA AI infrastructure. Under a multi-year $240M agreement between IBM and Together AI, IBM is positioned to deploy a large cluster of NVIDIA HGX B300 systems on IBM Cloud with expected availability in Q1 2027. Together AI will use this cluster to provide open-source model inference. This deployment is the first dedicated, large-scale cluster built for inference on IBM Cloud using HGX B300 systems and NVIDIA Spectrum - X TM Ethernet networking. According to NVIDIA, it is built to deliver 30x more AI factory output compared to prior generations.",
          "event_refs": [
